<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 5.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 5.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Vitoradis	 40,883   Feb 27    Mar 13     Dongkuk</p>
<p> Soldropt	  31,012   Feb 28    Mar 8	Inchon</p>
<p> Baltic Trident  55,000   Mar 11    Mar 20     Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Cargo	     39,311   Mar 17	-	  Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Transbridge     29,502   Mar 5     Mar 19     Kisco</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Joy Venture     38,500   Feb 28    Mar 17     Kangwon</p>
<p> Pac Duke	  25,000   Mar 7     Mar 22     POSCO</p>
<p> Fruition	  22,000   Late-Mar		 POSCO</p>
<p> T.B.N	     30,000   Mid-Apr		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule as yet</p>
</text>
